0065;16;556820;Chirrut's staff was a flame-hardened uneti-wood staff used as a walking stick and weapon by the blind monk Chirrut Îmwe. The staff had two handles of metal. One end of the staff was capped with an enclosure for a kyber crystal sliver, offering a symbolic source of inner illumination and allowing Îmwe to better gauge where the end of the staff was through the sound of the battery and crystal harmonic. During the Imperial occupation of Jedha's Holy City, Îmwe used the staff as a weapon against the Empire's stormtroopers, misleading his victims into believing the staff was merely a blind man's walking stick. Îmwe later went on to use the staff in the Battle of Scarif, where he was instrumental in the Rebel Alliance's successful theft of the Death Star plans.
0065;17;551180;After returning from Eadu, Jyn was called to a meeting of the Alliance leaders. Now possessing firm proof that the Empire had built a superweapon, the various leading Rebel politicians could not decide what to do about it, as most of them were terrified of the Death Star's destructive potential. Eventually, no decision was made, despite an impassioned plea from Jyn. This led Jyn, along with Cassian, Baze, Chirrut, Bodhi, K-2SO, and several volunteers, to go to Scarif against orders. The Citadel Tower on Scarif housed the Imperial archives, including a complete copy of the plans of the Death Star. The team, which dubbed themselves "Rogue One" on the fly, intended to infiltrate the facility and steal the plans. They passed through Scarif's Shield Gate in a stolen Imperial cargo ship, which had not yet been registered as stolen to the Empire. Upon landing, Jyn, Cassian and K-2SO infiltrated the tower itself, while the Rebel commandos who had come along staged a loud, noisy diversion. While this was going on, Rebel Command back on Yavin 4 eventually received word that there was fighting on Scarif, and immediately sent reinforcements. The fleet was led by Admiral Raddus from his flagship, the Profundity.
